      - Malta: Not banned. Source: [European Institute for Animal Law & Policy (2024-12).](https://animallaweurope.org/wp-content/uploads/Chick-and-Duckling-Killing-UPDATE-December-2024.pdf)
      - Poland: Not banned. Source: [European Institute for Animal Law & Policy (2024-12).](https://animallaweurope.org/wp-content/uploads/Chick-and-Duckling-Killing-UPDATE-December-2024.pdf)
      - Portugal: Not banned. Source: [European Institute for Animal Law & Policy (2024-12).](https://animallaweurope.org/wp-content/uploads/Chick-and-Duckling-Killing-UPDATE-December-2024.pdf)
      - Romania: Not banned. Source: [European Institute for Animal Law & Policy (2024-12).](https://animallaweurope.org/wp-content/uploads/Chick-and-Duckling-Killing-UPDATE-December-2024.pdf)
      - Slovakia: Not banned. Source: [European Institute for Animal Law & Policy (2024-12).](https://animallaweurope.org/wp-content/uploads/Chick-and-Duckling-Killing-UPDATE-December-2024.pdf)
      - Slovenia: Not banned. Source: [European Institute for Animal Law & Policy (2024-12).](https://animallaweurope.org/wp-content/uploads/Chick-and-Duckling-Killing-UPDATE-December-2024.pdf)
      - Spain: Not banned. Source: [European Institute for Animal Law & Policy (2024-12).](https://animallaweurope.org/wp-content/uploads/Chick-and-Duckling-Killing-UPDATE-December-2024.pdf)
      - Sweden: Not banned. Source: [European Institute for Animal Law & Policy (2024-12).](https://animallaweurope.org/wp-content/uploads/Chick-and-Duckling-Killing-UPDATE-December-2024.pdf)
